cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "CIF Density Calculator: a validated Jupyter notebook for theoretical density calculation from CIF files"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Galeazzi
    given-names: Cristian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7150-2659"
    affiliation: "Center for Materials Research (ZfM/LaMa), Justus Liebig University Giessen, Germany"
abstract: >-
  Computes the theoretical (crystallographic) density of every phase in a
  folder of CIF files and exports the results to CSV. Handles multi-block
  Rietveld exports, multi-phase files and partial site occupancies
  (vacancies, dopants, mixed sites), and isolates unreadable files without
  stopping the batch. Densities are validated against reference values
  computed independently from IUPAC standard atomic weights.
repository-code: "https://github.com/cristian-galeazzi/CIF-Density-Calculator"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-30
license: MIT
keywords:
  - crystallography
  - CIF
  - theoretical density
  - X-ray density
  - crystallographic density
  - unit cell
  - site occupancy
  - Rietveld
  - pymatgen
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Python Materials Genomics (pymatgen): A robust, open-source python library for materials analysis"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ong
        given-names: Shyue Ping
    journal: "Computational Materials Science"
    volume: 68
    start: 314
    end: 319
    year: 2013
    doi: 10.1016/j.commatsci.2012.10.028
